<title>USA: USDA wants to raise fees for grain inspections.</title>
<headline>USDA wants to raise fees for grain inspections.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department said it wants to increase fees by 12.5 percent for grain inspection and weighing services.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, the agency's Grain Inspection, Packers and Stockyards Administration said needs to raise fees to cover operational costs.</p>
<p>The agency said it would review comments about the plan that are submitted by August 18.</p>
<p>((-- Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
